From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Rouesnel <wrouesnel@wrouesnel.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:05:16 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] settings: Don't validate an empty TLS certificate path

The certificate path setting is an empty string until a certificate
is configured, and every grdctl call or daemon start then tried to
load it, logging that the certificate is invalid:

  [ERROR][com.freerdp.crypto] - [x509_utils_from_pem]: BIO_new failed for certificate
  RDP server certificate is invalid.

That happens on every clean setup, so a real certificate problem
can't be told apart from it in the journal. Treat an empty path as
no certificate.

(cherry picked from commit 6f17b5fc740bae5fcc9606380df850d16b481088)
---
 src/grd-settings.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/grd-settings.c b/src/grd-settings.c
index 3da3df3..2ac1d2e 100644
--- a/src/grd-settings.c
+++ b/src/grd-settings.c
@@ -475,7 +475,7 @@ update_rdp_server_fingerprint (GrdSettings *settings)
 #endif
   g_autofree char *fingerprint = NULL;
 
-  if (!priv->rdp.server_cert_path)
+  if (!priv->rdp.server_cert_path || !*priv->rdp.server_cert_path)
     return;
 
 #ifdef HAVE_RDP
